WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  the rallies united brazilians from all  ages and walks of life  trade union leaders and left-wing  politicians standing side by side with  businessmen bankers and students  we have created a great front if we want  to defend brazil's democracy from  president gerbal sonora's attacks  this is a unique moment when businessmen  and workers join efforts to defend  democracy the main rally was at the  university of sao paulo's law school  where a similar event was held 45 years  ago against brazil's military  dictatorship  crowds gathered inside the building and  in the courtyard to listen to two  manifestos both defending brazil's  democratic institutions less than two  months before october's presidential  elections  our democracy is facing immense danger  our institutions are at risk from  insinuations and contempt for the  results of the elections the manifestos  were drawn up after president jaime  bolsonaro stepped up his attacks on  brazil's supreme court an electronic  voting system  in july he told a group of foreign  ambassadors that the elections could be  easily rigged  polls show bolsonaro trailing behind  former president luiz nassulullah  the movement in defense of brazil's  democracy grew over the past weeks  spreading to at least 20 state capitals  among them rio de janeiro crowds  gathered at universities here in rio and  in other cities to listen to the  manifestos being read  people here say they must show their  unity on the streets to ensure that  democracy and the rule of law prevail  manika yanakiv al-jazeera rio de janeiro

